      "side": 1,
      "message": "I actually don\u0027t like this change. The existing format is more inline with Python style without the extra spaces.\n\nSo then I tried fiddling with pdftoin_shrdlu.py, and it turned out my OS for some reason did not provide mutools. I do have an older copy of the mupdf source laying around, so I actually had a mutools binary ready to go, except that didn\u0027t work. I synced my mupdf source, rebuilt, and got it working.\n\nThis make me realize a couple of things:\n\n1. Having more external dependencies is annoying in its own way.\n2. The external dependency can change its behavior at any time / different versions may not format consistently.\n\nI haven\u0027t had the energy to work on this, but I\u0027m hoping maybe with some AI help, the script can become self-contained.",
      "revId": "6d8c847882a8140cd94e5abb49fe8a084db534cb",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
